diff --git a/docs/ops/logging.md b/docs/ops/logging.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..80306ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Logging & ops alerting
+
+PegaFila splits observability into three lanes. Pick the one that matches the
+question you are answering.
+
+## Lanes
+
+### 1. Archive — routine application logs
+
+- **Channel:** `daily` (driver `daily`, `storage/logs/laravel.log`, 14 days).
+- **Level:** `LOG_LEVEL` (default `debug`).
+- **Use for:** debug/info/warning/error messages about normal application flow
+  (requests, jobs, cache misses, validation failures). Rotated daily.
+- **API:** `Log::debug(...)`, `Log::info(...)`, ... or the default channel.
+
+### 2. Audit — durable "who changed/tried what" trail
+
+- **Channel:** `audit` (driver `daily`, `storage/logs/audit.log`, 90 days,
+  minimum `info`).
+- **Use for:** security-relevant or accountability events: membership role
+  changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts, permission denials, manual
+  overrides. Written by the code that performs the action.
+- **API:** `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [...])`.
+
+### 3. Alert — human-pageable ops incidents (Discord)
+
+- **Mechanism:** explicit call, **not** a Monolog channel. Class
+  `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert`, method `send(string $title, string $message, array $context = [])`.
+- **Use for:** actionable breakage that warrants waking someone up: a job that
+  exhausted retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an
+  entity. Do **not** use for routine errors.
+- **Config:** `services.discord.webhook_url` (env `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`). Empty
+  value disables it (silent no-op, no HTTP request).
+- **Behaviour:** POSTs `{"content": "..."}` to the webhook with a short timeout.
+  Text is `title`, `message`, then `key=value` lines, truncated to 1800 chars.
+  Sensitive keys/values are redacted. Never throws; failures are logged via
+  `Log::error('Discord ops alert failed', ...)`.
+
+## Decision guide
+
+| Situation | Lane |
+| --- | --- |
+| "Something happened, might be useful later" | Archive (`Log::...`) |
+| "Who did what, for compliance/audit" | Audit (`Log::channel('audit')`) |
+| "Wake someone up now" | Alert (`DiscordOpsAlert::send`) |
+| Routine validation/not-found | Archive (debug/info), or no log at all |
+
+## Rules
+
+- Discord is **never** a Monolog channel and must not be added to `config/logging.php`.
+- Redact secrets in alert context; the notifier does this automatically for
+  sensitive keys and bearer tokens.
+- Keep audit entries factual and structured (include actor, entity, before/after).
+- Do not log secrets or PII to any lane.
\ No newline at end of file
